      "source": [
        "### 🧩 FastText Parameters Explained\n",
        "\n",
        "| Parameter       | Meaning              | Explanation (in simple words) |\n",
        "|-----------------|--------------------|-------------------------------|\n",
        "| `corpus`        | Input data  (sentence)        | The list of tokenized sentences (each sentence as a list of words). This is the text data the model learns from. |\n",
        "| `vector_size=50`| Size of each word vector | Each word will be represented as a 50-dimensional numeric vector. <br>→ Higher values capture more meaning but require more data & memory. |\n",
        "| `window=2`      | Context window size | The model looks at 2 words before and after the target word to understand its context. <br>→ Example: In “I love machine learning”, the context of “machine” includes “love” and “learning”. |\n",
        "| `min_count=1`   | Minimum word frequency | Words that appear fewer times than this are ignored. <br>→ Setting `1` means even rare words are included. |\n",
        "| `sg=1`          | Training algorithm   | `sg=1` → Skip-Gram model (predicts context from a target word). <br>`sg=0` → CBOW model (predicts target word from context). <br>Skip-Gram works better for rare words. |\n"
      ]
